WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.082
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade twelve English.

2
00:00:06.382 --> 00:00:09.896
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.196 --> 00:00:17.655
Unit seven: Relative Clauses: Defining and Non-defining. Today you will add information with who, which, that and whose.

4
00:00:17.955 --> 00:00:20.560
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.965
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.817 --> 00:00:26.818
Relative.

7
00:00:27.817 --> 00:00:30.060
Relative means connecting information.

8
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.313
Who is a relative pronoun.

9
00:00:32.917 --> 00:00:35.488
Your turn. Say: Relative.

10
00:00:38.333 --> 00:00:39.369
Relative.

11
00:00:40.117 --> 00:00:41.095
Defining.

12
00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:44.489
Defining means necessary to identify.

13
00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:47.303
A defining clause is essential.

14
00:00:47.917 --> 00:00:50.581
Your turn. Say: Defining.

15
00:00:53.433 --> 00:00:54.272
Defining.

16
00:00:55.017 --> 00:00:56.169
Non-defining.

17
00:00:57.183 --> 00:00:59.659
Non-defining means extra information.

18
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.843
It is shown with commas.

19
00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:05.381
Your turn. Say: Non-defining.

20
00:01:08.233 --> 00:01:09.432
Non-defining.

21
00:01:10.183 --> 00:01:10.941
Whose.

22
00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:13.659
Whose means showing possession.

23
00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:15.855
The girl whose bag is red.

24
00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:18.626
Your turn. Say: Whose.

25
00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:22.201
Whose.

26
00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:23.638
Whom.

27
00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.591
Whom means object form of who.

28
00:01:27.183 --> 00:01:28.568
The man whom I met.

29
00:01:29.183 --> 00:01:31.720
Your turn. Say: Whom.

30
00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:35.185
Whom.

31
00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:36.823
Omit.

32
00:01:37.817 --> 00:01:39.445
Omit means to leave out.

33
00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:41.248
You can omit that.

34
00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:44.560
Your turn. Say: Omit.

35
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.157
Omit.

36
00:01:48.917 --> 00:01:49.628
Comma.

37
00:01:50.617 --> 00:01:52.593
Comma means a punctuation mark.

38
00:01:53.183 --> 00:01:54.660
Use a comma here.

39
00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:57.252
Your turn. Say: Comma.

40
00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.031
Comma.

41
00:02:01.783 --> 00:02:02.703
Neighbour.

42
00:02:03.717 --> 00:02:06.030
Neighbour means a person living nearby.

43
00:02:06.617 --> 00:02:08.059
My neighbour is kind.

44
00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:11.070
Your turn. Say: Neighbour.

45
00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:14.876
Neighbour.

46
00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:19.410
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:23.027
Visal, what is a defining relative clause?

48
00:02:24.117 --> 00:02:36.196
It gives necessary information that identifies the noun: The student who sits next to me is Sok. We do not use commas, and we can use that instead of who or which.

49
00:02:37.283 --> 00:02:38.818
And a non-defining one?

50
00:02:39.917 --> 00:02:51.764
It gives extra information and uses commas: My brother, who lives in Kampot, is a teacher. We cannot use that and we cannot omit the pronoun.

51
00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:54.687
When can I leave the pronoun out?

52
00:02:55.783 --> 00:03:05.202
In a defining clause, you can omit who, which or that when it is the object: The book that I read was good, or The book I read was good.

53
00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:07.960
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:08.817 --> 00:03:12.372
Grammar focus: who and which and that and whose.

55
00:03:12.672 --> 00:03:13.894
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:14.583 --> 00:03:16.908
The student who sits next to me is Sok.

57
00:03:17.817 --> 00:03:20.757
My brother, who lives in Kampot, is a teacher.

58
00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:28.393
Use who for people, which for things and whose for possession. Non-defining clauses need commas and cannot use that.

59
00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:33.277
Be careful! Don't say: My brother, that lives in Kampot, is kind.

60
00:03:35.233 --> 00:03:38.278
Say: My brother, who lives in Kampot, is kind.

61
00:03:38.578 --> 00:03:40.066
No that after a comma.

62
00:03:40.867 --> 00:03:43.577
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:45.484
My Neighbours.

64
00:03:45.784 --> 00:03:48.097
The woman who lives next door is a nurse.

65
00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.552
Her son, who is ten, plays football.

66
00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:54.647
The house that they bought is near the river.

67
00:03:55.633 --> 00:03:58.724
Their dog, which is very friendly, barks at strangers.

68
00:03:59.733 --> 00:04:02.186
They are a family whose kindness I admire.

69
00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:07.371
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:08.217 --> 00:04:09.694
Who is used for blank.

71
00:04:09.994 --> 00:04:13.543
A, places. B, people. C, things.

72
00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.914
The answer is B: people.

73
00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:21.968
Non-defining clauses use blank.

74
00:04:22.268 --> 00:04:25.759
A, no commas. B, brackets. C, commas.

75
00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.300
The answer is C: commas.

76
00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:34.740
The girl blank bag is red is my friend.

77
00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.171
A, whose. B, who. C, which.

78
00:04:41.733 --> 00:04:43.628
The answer is A: whose.

79
00:04:44.783 --> 00:04:46.969
That can be used in a blank clause.

80
00:04:47.269 --> 00:04:51.050
A, both. B, defining. C, non-defining.

81
00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.356
The answer is B: defining.

82
00:04:57.517 --> 00:04:58.912
Which is used for blank.

83
00:04:59.212 --> 00:05:02.320
A, people. B, names. C, things.

84
00:05:05.867 --> 00:05:07.715
The answer is C: things.

85
00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:11.796
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:14.557
Describe a person using who.

87
00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:24.665
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:24.965 --> 00:05:34.864
My teacher is a person who always encourages us. She explains difficult lessons clearly. I respect her because she never gives up on her students.

89
00:05:35.164 --> 00:05:36.978
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:37.883 --> 00:05:42.556
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and who and which and that and whose.

91
00:05:42.856 --> 00:05:47.946
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

92
00:05:48.246 --> 00:05:50.678
See you in Unit eight. Goodbye!

93
00:05:50.978 --> 00:05:53.990
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

